Five rules I want to remember
DNS client asks; DNS server answers.
127.0.0.1 means "this computer," not "the Domain Controller."
10.10.10.10 is ADDC01's reachable address from other machines in the lab.
DNS tells machines where AD services are; DNS does not route the actual traffic.
DNS finds the service; AD stores identity information; Kerberos authenticates the identity.
